{"claims":[{"claim_text":"The President has worked to help states develop new approaches to expand coverage in their Medicaid and State Children's Health Insurance Program (SCHIP) programs.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Waivers and state plan amendments approved by the Department of Health and Human Services have expanded eligibility under Medicaid and SCHIP programs to more than 2.6 million children since 2001.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Waivers and state plan amendments approved by the Department of Health and Human Services have improved benefits for more than 8 million children and adults since 2001.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The Bush Administration is fostering the creation of innovative approaches to health care access and delivery by the states by working with governors of both parties.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Support for enhancing efforts to reach the parents of children who are eligible for the State Children's Health Insurance Program (SCHIP) so that more children receive health coverage.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The President proposed a refundable tax credit that will make health insurance more affordable to millions of Americans who do not have employer-provided insurance or public insurance.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"The Treasury Department estimates the tax credit will extend insurance to between four and five million Americans.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"The Trade Promotion Authority bill, supported by the Republican Congress and signed by President Bush, provides a tax credit to help workers obtain health insurance coverage if they have lost their jobs due to international trade.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[5]},{"claim_text":"The tax credit provided by the Trade Promotion Authority bill has helped thousands of displaced workers get insurance coverage.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[5]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
